# Response headers for static assets, applied by Workers Static Assets.
#
# This file is the asset half of a pair: it cannot reach responses built by
# worker/index.ts, which stamps the same security headers in code. The two
# lists are asserted identical by scripts/verify/repo-config.test.mjs.
#
# Lives in public/ so vite copies it to dist/client, which is the configured
# assets directory. Wrangler parses it at deploy time and does not serve it.

# The headers the Traefik `security` middleware used to apply at the ingress.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none

# Content-hashed build output: the URL changes whenever the bytes change, so
# the response never expires. Everything else keeps the Static Assets default
# of `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, revalidated cheaply by its ETag -
# the same two cache classes the Go server assigned from AssetPrefix.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
